  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img height=\"100\" src=\"assets\\st0184_660879171f78.png\" width=\"828\" /><br /><br />Addition of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>NO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> is an electrophilic addition. The <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math> increases the electron density on the left benzene ring, whereas the carbonyl group decreases the charge density of the right benzene group. As a result, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>NO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> is added to the left benzene group due to higher charge density.</p>"
